{"answer": "**Budget Numbers Thread \u2013 Participants & Commitments**\n\n| Participant | Email | Commitment |\n|-------------|-------|------------|\n| **Alice Ander** (ct\u2011alice) | alice@company.com | None specified as a task in this thread. (She requested that proposals be added by Thursday and highlighted that \u201cOff\u2011site is already committed.\u201d) |\n| **Bobby** (ct\u2011bob) | bob@company.com | Will take \u201ctravel scenarios\u201d *(msg\u201120: \u201cI will take travel scenarios.\u201d)* |\n| **Carol Corte** (ct\u2011carol) | carol@company.com | Will take \u201ctooling\u201d *(msg\u201119: \u201cWill do. I will take tooling.\u201d)* |\n| **You** (ct\u2011self) | you@company.com | 1. Pull contractor breakdown tomorrow *(msg\u201115: \u201cI will pull the contractor breakdown tomorrow.\u201d)* <br>2. Reconcile against last quarter *(msg\u201121: \u201cAnd I will reconcile against last quarter.\u201d)* |\n\n### How we derived this\n\n- The **conversation@1** projection was read from `messages/thread/thr-group` (content hash **5cb6b24dc8ed7ae34615e3497492f739052db9b3bce0d717f861c20569198e89**).  \n- The extracted message bodies were parsed for explicit commitment language (e.g., \u201cI will \u2026\u201d).  \n- Participant identities were mapped to the `sender_id` values (`ct\u2011alice`, `ct\u2011bob`, `ct\u2011carol`, `ct\u2011self`) and resolved to contact labels (`Alice Ander`, `Bobby`, `Carol Corte`, `You`).  \n- The task prompt hash (**d4ea6e6d230d1ee051ba3237af6bb16df6fa20bc7721a155db83ac37fef920c4**) is used to satisfy provenance requirements for this answer.\n\nThese are the only explicit task commitments recorded in the thread.", "answer_hash": "1460bb37403327ea8354f13c87aa6732579cc85f76adda25a47da0c4c6c787dc", "kind": "task_end", "receipt_id": "r-84", "seq": 84, "task_id": "t2-group-thread-resolution", "truncated": false, "ts": 1105.0}
